{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CegA33LJ2oM4RqTvQ9mF5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Bop4YbtYAXiq5TDvbLRP1S","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/diytechy/.claude/projects/-Users-diytechy-Documents-ai-template/memory/verify-inherited-fixes-paired-readers.md","content":"---\nname: verify-inherited-fixes-paired-readers\ndescription: Re-drive a rework finding's already-landed fix instead of reading it; tightening one of two paired readers silently wedges the other\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nWhen a worker session inherits a REWORK FINDING that a prior commit on the same\nbranch already fixed, **re-drive the fix rather than confirm it by reading the\ndiff**. On WI-579 the round-022 MAJOR was closed at `c939d49c`; driving it on\nthe suite's own fixture surfaced a NEW major defect the fix itself introduced.\n\nThe specific trap, which recurred three times on one lane (rounds 007, 015,\n022→023): where two readers answer one question from two sides — the merge gate\n(`integrate._verdict_gate`) and the loop's owed-derivation\n(`agent_loop.review_owed_by_evidence`) — **tightening one silently wedges the\nlane**, because the other still clears on the looser rule. The lane then\nschedules nothing while the gate refuses, or draws a round the gate won't read.\n\n**Why:** a passing suite proves neither reader wrong; the disagreement is only\nvisible when you drive BOTH at the same fixture state and compare answers.\n\n**How to apply:** write a scratch test that calls both readers on one fixture\nand asserts they agree, before touching anything. Then put the shared rule in\nthe leaf both import (here `kitlib/verdict.py`) — and when the two questions are\nlegitimately different (drawn-vs-approved), say so in the docstring and pin the\ndivergence class in a test, rather than forcing a false unity. Related:\n[[rederive-dont-rerun-measured-claims]],\n[[stale-not-discharged-clauses-on-approved-rows]].\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":217,"cache_read_input_tokens":189936,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":217},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c77d95a-257c-47ee-9c6a-bf0d0ac81ad1","uuid":"50b90961-5d10-4608-9c20-c32711c3a268","request_id":"req_011CegA328cfUerrMgxUkgHj"}
