ers on one fixture\nand asserts they agree, before touching anything. Then put the shared rule in\nthe leaf both import (here `kitlib/verdict.py`) — and when the two questions are\nlegitimately different (drawn-vs-approved), say so in the docstring and pin the\ndivergence class in a test, rather than forcing a false unity. Related:\n[[rederive-dont-rerun-measured-claims]],\n[[stale-not-discharged-clauses-on-approved-rows]].\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
