{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CegA4vowdNKkgoBQm211R","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"WI-579 round 023 is closed. Two commits, both trailered `WI: WI-579`, tree clean.\n\n## What happened\n\n**The assigned rework findings were already fixed** by `c939d49c` (an earlier commit on this branch). Rather than confirm that by reading the diff, I re-drove it — and the verification found a new MAJOR defect *introduced by that fix*.\n\n**The defect.** Round 022 taught `integrate._verdict_gate` to demand every phase the `review_rounds` dial declares. But `agent_loop.review_owed_by_evidence` still read \"any verdict at this tree means the round was served\", and the review phase queue is in-memory run state. Driven on the suite's own policy-2 fixture with REVIEW-A served:\n\n```\nloop says round owed: False\ngate says: wi-401: the governing round(s) at this tree are not an APPROVE (REVIEW-B)\n```\n\nA run killed between REVIEW-A and REVIEW-B resumes scheduling nothing, against a gate refusing the merge for a phase nobody will ever draw. This repo runs `review_rounds = 1` so it was never live here — the kit ships 2 as the recommended pairing, so it was live downstream.\n\n**The fix.** `kitlib/verdict.py` gains the count dimension beside the identity one: `declared_phases` (the span both readers slice, clamped — a negative policy would otherwise slice from the end) and `phases_owed` (which declared phases a tree never had *drawn*). `review_owed_by_evidence` returns those phases instead of a flag; `resume_owed_round` queues only them, so it completes the same round rather than redrawing a served phase — which the gate would read as a reroll-until-green.\n\n**One divergence is deliberate and stated, not papered over:** `phases_owed` asks whether a phase was drawn; the gate asks whether it produced a parseable APPROVE. They must differ on exactly one class — a present-but-unparseable verdict — and a pure test pins that.\n\n## Bars (measured, not claimed)\n\n- Smoke: **1510 passed, 8 skipped in 31.92 s**; enforced rerun **33.4 s against the 60 s ceiling**; `check_docs --stale` **0 broken links**.\n- Full unfiltered suite: **3349 passed, 24 skipped, 1 failed in 616.89 s**. The sole red is `test_derive_stage.py::test_this_repo_s_committed_stage_is_current` — the branch-caused, trunk-owned `docs/stage` fingerprint handoff bisected against the integration base in an earlier round; `docs/stage` is untouched by this branch.\n\n## Two things worth flagging\n\n- **`agent_loop.py` took a reviewed +1 SLOC ratchet bump** (2578→2579) — one real line, the `owed` binding. Reason recorded at the baseline entry and in the log.\n- **A residual I did not act on:** a resumed round's in-memory `round_verdicts` holds only the redrawn phases, so if the already-served phase had *dissented*, the loop attempts a merge the gate then refuses by name. Fail-closed and visible; seeding it would mean inventing the dead session's family/model. Recorded in the fragment so an adjudicator can rule rather than rediscover.\n\nSpine touched: LLR-207, IF-175, TC-205 — all `Drafted` and authored by this branch, no Approved cell amended. `docs/ratify/CURRENT.md` regenerated. I did **not** perform any approval act. TC-205 also picked up round 022's own regression, which that commit added to the suite but never listed in the case's evidence.\n\nThe branch's non-record tree changed, so the merge queue will want a fresh verdict round — that's the coordinator's to schedule, not mine."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":565,"cache_read_input_tokens":191638,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":565},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0c77d95a-257c-47ee-9c6a-bf0d0ac81ad1","uuid":"1d79167c-b028-479b-a521-b055a0b71b3c","request_id":"req_011CegA4uXZ5cVmukjimrZ3n"}
